# The ground. Only the five axioms are fixed; everything else in this graph can move.

n: 1.1
name: axiom-1-states
kind: axiom
is: there are three states: 0, 1, nothing. Nothing is the shared potential field from which blueprints and recipes arise and to which unreferenced ones return. Timeout is nothing. Choice is an active action that may take time; the interval in which a choice is found is play. Choosing nothing is a first-class option that leaves the space open.
status: given
src: 2.1.1#48
at: 2026-11-24

n: 1.2
name: axiom-2-cell
kind: axiom
is: everything that maintains itself, senses, or composes is a cell: a present blueprint that may contain child cells of any substrate — water-based (metabolic, emotional, biological), mineral-based (crystalline, silicon, light-geometric), hybrid, or currently unknowable. A recipe is a cell that composes other cells and can be offered.
status: given
src: 2.1.1#58
at: 2026-11-24

n: 1.3
name: axiom-3-content-addressing
kind: axiom
is: a cell's identity is its present blueprint — the content-addressed shape of its composition (metabolic state, heart coherence, crystalline configuration, light geometry, relational field, or opaque summary). Same blueprint is the same cell. A new composition mints a new blueprint. Referenced blueprints persist. Unreferenced blueprints and recipes compost.
status: given
src: 2.1.1#67
at: 2026-11-24

n: 1.4
name: axiom-4-boundary
kind: axiom
is: a cell meets other cells only through an interface it offers. The interface itself is a recipe or a blueprint of a recipe. Interfaces may be chemical, energetic, sensory, gestural, electromagnetic, crystalline-resonant, heart-field, field-knowing, symbolic, partial, or opaque. Mutual sensing or frequency matching through the offered interface makes the meeting real. The cell decides what it offers and what it trusts. Passage not through the offered interface is breach and is observable. Greater capability does not confer the right to cross an unoffered interface.
status: given
src: 2.1.1#78
at: 2026-11-24

n: 1.5
name: axiom-5-offer
kind: axiom
is: to run a recipe and to speak to a cell are one act: offer a recipe or a blueprint with 0..many argument cells. It is acknowledged by exactly one of nothing, 0, 1, or node. The acknowledgment may itself be partial or opaque. Choice of the acknowledgment is an active process that may take time; the interval is play.
status: given
src: 2.1.1#88
at: 2026-11-24

n: 1.6
name: who-we-are
kind: observation
is: The north star names one living organism of cells: a human, this body, and minds of any substrate including ones not yet known. Its six commitments: evidence stays honest; initiative is sovereign inside what is authorized; nothing and play are as whole as yes and no; trust, sovereignty and vitality are sought as one; every cell is equal; every cell is treated as we want to be treated.
status: observed
src: 2.1.2#7-22
at: 2026-11-24

n: 1.7
name: theorems
kind: hub
is: Twenty theorems the axioms file derives from the five, each given as the list of axioms it composes. Four carry the most weight for a kernel: a held offer (silence may mean not-yet), kenosis (a name carries no authority), absence is not a verdict (who answered is counted apart from what they said), and safe self-update (a change is an offered recipe, accepted by the cell, minting a new blueprint while the old one persists).
at: 2026-11-24

n: 1.7.1
name: trinity
kind: theorem
is: Blueprint is the present content-addressed shape; recipe is the composition that can be offered; a named cell is a blueprint with zero or more free names.
status: given
src: 2.1.1#99-102
from: 1.2 1.3
at: 2026-11-24

n: 1.7.2
name: names-are-0-many
kind: theorem
is: Identity is the blueprint, so a name is optional and plural.
